From f7f0763afc06da70479c3c0e6453620f2baf78f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:59:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor SCE-latch recovery (clear frame +
 escalation) and bursted CLU11 cancel

Route 11c forensics: during commanded engagements the pedal latched FAULT_SCE (state 3, passthrough) from CAN error
frames caused by our 100 Hz CLU11 CANCEL colliding with the cluster's own 50 Hz CLU11; only an ENABLE=0 zero frame
clears it, so the pedal applied 6.56 s of 55.1 s commanded (11.9 %).

FIX 1 (gas_interceptor.py PedalFaultMonitor): while commanding, if the pedal's broadcast STATE is nonzero, the 50 Hz
send slot carries one ENABLE=0 zero frame instead (counter continuous, valid CRC; costs no torque, the pedal is already
in passthrough), at most once per 60 ms. Escalation: fault visible > 0.5 s or > 8 clears in 2 s -> CarState.accFaulted
(standard "Cruise Fault" immediate disable), held until longitudinal disengages.
Plumbing: CarStateExt owns the monitor next to interceptor_state; that CarState instance is the CS passed to
create_gas_command, so the controller reads STATE and latches escalation on it, and CarStateExt.update reports it on
the next frame. No capnp/schema change; inert unless CP_SP.enableGasInterceptor.

FIX 2 (carcontroller.py, gas interceptor only): CLU11 CANCEL after the existing 10-frame delay is sent as 5-frame
bursts with rotating 150/200/250 ms pauses (20 % duty) instead of every frame. Stock pcmCruise cars and the CAN FD
path are unchanged.
